<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48693" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trăgoedus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τραγῳδός.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A tragic actor</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen.
				3, 2, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 1, 28, 128</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 12,
				5, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 2, 129</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Tragoedus,
				<i>an epithet of Jupiter</i>, derived from the
			Vicus Tragoedus at Rome, in the Regio Esquilina, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Aug. 57</span></i>; Sext. <i><span class="en">Ruf. Reg.
		5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
